    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "An Exciting Redevelopment Opportunity Beside Norman Gardens\r\n\r\n22 Maiden Lane occupies one of the most remarkable settings in New Ross Town, the semi-derelict cottage stands on a generous c. 950sq m (0.23 acre) plot beside the Norman Gardens and enjoys elevated and panoramic views across the rooftops of the town, the River Barrow and the surrounding countryside. While the existing cottage requires complete refurbishment or redevelopment (subject to the necessary planning permission), the site offers exceptional potential for those seeking to create a distinctive home or to explore its commercial possibilities.\r\n\r\nOUTSIDE:  Terraced grounds which extend to c. 950sq m (0.23 acre)\r\nBER: Exempt \r\nEIRCODE: Y34Y228"
      },
      {
